.IX Title "Lucy::Index::IndexReader 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Index::IndexReader 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Index::IndexReader \- Read from an inverted index.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 10
\&    my $reader = Lucy::Index::IndexReader\->open(
\&        index => \*(Aq/path/to/index\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&    my $seg_readers = $reader\->seg_readers;
\&    for my $seg_reader (@$seg_readers) {
\&        my $seg_name = $seg_reader\->get_segment\->get_name;
\&        my $num_docs = $seg_reader\->doc_max;
\&        print "Segment $seg_name ($num_docs documents):\en";
\&        my $doc_reader = $seg_reader\->obtain("Lucy::Index::DocReader");
\&        for my $doc_id ( 1 .. $num_docs ) {
\&            my $doc = $doc_reader\->fetch_doc($doc_id);
\&            print "  $doc_id: $doc\->{title}\en";
\&        }
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
IndexReader is the interface through which
IndexSearcher objects access the
content of an index.
.PP
IndexReader objects always represent a point-in-time view of an index as it
existed at the moment the reader was created.  If you want search results
to reflect modifications to an index, you must create a new IndexReader
after the update process completes.
.PP
IndexReaders are composites; most of the work is done by individual
DataReader sub-components, which may be
accessed via \fBfetch()\fR and \fBobtain()\fR.  The most efficient and powerful access
to index data happens at the segment level via
SegReader’s sub-components.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS open
.IX Subsection "open"
.Vb 5
\&    my $reader = Lucy::Index::IndexReader\->open(
\&        index    => \*(Aq/path/to/index\*(Aq, # required
\&        snapshot => $snapshot,
\&        manager  => $index_manager,
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
IndexReader is an abstract base class; \fBopen()\fR returns the IndexReader
subclass PolyReader, which channels the output of 0 or more SegReaders.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBindex\fR \- Either a string filepath or a Folder.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsnapshot\fR \- A Snapshot.  If not supplied, the most recent snapshot
file will be used.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBmanager\fR \- An IndexManager.
Read-locking is off by default; supplying this argument turns it on.
.SH "ABSTRACT METHODS"
.IX Header "ABSTRACT METHODS"
.SS doc_max
.IX Subsection "doc_max"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $index_reader\->doc_max();
.Ve
.PP
Return the maximum number of documents available to the reader, which
is also the highest possible internal document id.  Documents which
have been marked as deleted but not yet purged from the index are
included in this count.
.SS doc_count
.IX Subsection "doc_count"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $index_reader\->doc_count();
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of documents available to the reader, subtracting
any that are marked as deleted.
.SS del_count
.IX Subsection "del_count"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $index_reader\->del_count();
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of documents which have been marked as deleted but
not yet purged from the index.
.SS offsets
.IX Subsection "offsets"
.Vb 1
\&    my $i32_array = $index_reader\->offsets();
.Ve
.PP
Return an array with one entry for each segment, corresponding to
segment doc_id start offset.
.SS seg_readers
.IX Subsection "seg_readers"
.Vb 1
\&    my $arrayref = $index_reader\->seg_readers();
.Ve
.PP
Return an array of all the SegReaders represented within the
IndexReader.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS obtain
.IX Subsection "obtain"
.Vb 1
\&    my $data_reader = $index_reader\->obtain($api);
.Ve
.PP
Fetch a component, or throw an error if the component can’t be found.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBapi\fR \- The name of the DataReader subclass that the desired
component must implement.
.SS fetch
.IX Subsection "fetch"
.Vb 1
\&    my $data_reader = $index_reader\->fetch($api);
.Ve
.PP
Fetch a component, or return undef if the component can’t be
found.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBapi\fR \- The name of the DataReader subclass that the desired
component must implement.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Index::IndexReader isa Lucy::Index::DataReader isa Clownfish::Obj.
